      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that excluding the \"working poor\" creates a system that feels unjust to the average struggling family, and that is exactly why a rigid, narrow definition of \"vulnerability\" is a failure of policy. True equity requires us to expand the income eligibility threshold to include those who are struggling but not destitute, rather than creating a two-tier system that leaves the majority of renters behind. We must redefine \"need\" to encompass anyone facing financial instability, ensuring the mandate actually helps the broad community instead of just a select few.",
